From ee6498b4b9ac9ca19887d78d21632a8f70ec6fae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Gifford <mike.gifford@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:28:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add ExtensionFileValidator and the ex:validate command

A malformed .info.yml file stops the container build once caches are
cleared, even when the extension is not installed. The new validator
checks info files with InfoParserDynamic and Symfony YAML, plus PECL
YAML when it is loaded. It also checks value types, file names, base
themes and PHP syntax. It needs no installed site.

The ex:validate command runs it for continuous integration and before
a deployment. Options: --changed, --include-tests, --php-lint, --strict and
--format=json.
